      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "To which of the following sets do all the negative integers belong?\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We must check whether each set contains all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{N}$ contains the positive integers (natural numbers). For instance, $-1$ is in the given class but not in $\\mathbb{N}$. Therefore, this set does not contain all the negative integers.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Z}$ contains all integers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Z}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$ contains the negative rational numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$.\n\n- The set $\\mathbb{R}$ contains all real numbers. By the number-set hierarchy and the sign restrictions, every member of the given class belongs to $\\mathbb{R}$.\n\nTherefore, select $\\mathbb{Z}$, $\\mathbb{Q}^{-}$, $\\mathbb{R}$ only.",
